Thu Nov 19 00:18:43 UTC 2026 - Matej Cepl <mcepl@cepl.eu>

- Update to 2.0.0:
  gt 2.0.0 brings gt's flags and JSON output in line with gh,
  keeps settings and stored tokens readable across versions,
  works with narrowly scoped CI tokens, and fixes many bugs.
  - Breaking changes
    - --json and --csv require a field list. Like gh, --json
      without fields fails with a usage error that lists the
      available fields. Use --jq . or --template to read every
      field. gt no longer guesses whether the word after --json
      is a field list or an argument (#127).
    - Absent values in JSON are null. A field without a value is
      now null instead of "" or a missing key, an empty list is
      [], and every declared field is always present. Timestamps
      are RFC 3339 in UTC to the second. Fields that cost extra
      requests, such as reviewers or blocked_by, are read only
      when --json names them or the --jq/--template expression
      mentions them (#127).
    - gt pr merge uses gh's flag names: --message is now --body
      (-b), --message-file is --body-file (-F) and --title is
      --subject (-t). -s is now --squash instead of --method, and
      --merge and --rebase gain -m and -r. --method stays,
      long-only, for Gitea's other merge styles (#125).
    - Renamed or removed flags, matching gh (#126):
    - Teams are requested as ORG/TEAM in pr create --reviewer, pr
      edit --add-reviewer/--remove-reviewer and pr review
      request/cancel-request --reviewer. --reviewer-team,
      --add-reviewer-team, --remove-reviewer-team and --team are
      removed.
    - pr create --allow-maintainer-edits is now
      --no-maintainer-edit.
    - search issue|pr replaces --assigned, --authored and
      --mentioned with --assignee, --author and --mentions, which
      take a user or @me.
    - repo edit --actions is now --enable-actions, and repo edit
      --private is removed in favour of --visibility.
    - The hidden --before of gt notification is removed; use
      --until.
    - gt issue edit and gt pr edit rename
      --add-blocks/--remove-blocks to gh's
      --add-blocking/--remove-blocking (#99).
    - Plain output is smaller for scripts and agents: job logs
      print without Gitea's per-line timestamp (--timestamps
      keeps it), run logs --failed and run view --log-failed
      print only the failed steps, and piped lists shorten commit
      IDs to twelve characters and drop the URL column where the
      row already identifies the item (#115).
    - Tokens in the system keyring move to the service
      gitea-cli:HOST[/PATH] with the account name, so they can be
      found in Keychain Access and similar tools. Existing tokens
      are moved the first time 2.0 uses them; gt 1.x cannot read
      moved tokens (#124).
    - gt config set with an unknown key now stores it with a
      warning instead of failing (#124).
    - A 403 for a missing token scope now exits 4
      (authentication) instead of 1 (#123).
    - Polling commands (run watch, run logs --follow, workflow
      run --follow, pr checks --watch, notification watch)
      require --interval of at least 1s (#122).
    - go install is no longer a supported way to install gt: the
      module stays at gitea.dev/cli, so go install …@latest keeps
      resolving to 1.x. Use a release binary, a package or the
      install script (#118).
  - Features
    - gt issue create --blocked-by and --blocking set
      dependencies on the new issue, gt label list takes
      --search, --sort, --order and --web, and gt repo list takes
      --visibility, --archived, --no-archived, --topic and
      --language (#99).
    - Settings files from a later gt, or with settings this
      version does not know, are read and kept when gt rewrites
      them, so several gt versions can share one configuration
      (#124).
    - A GITEA_TOKEN without the read:user scope now works for
      every command that does not need to know whose token it is,
      and so does the git credential helper. gt auth login --help
      and gt help environment explain which scopes a token needs
      (#123).
    - Issue and pull request JSON gains locked, and pull request
      JSON gains pinned. gt pr view tells a deleted head branch
      or open blockers apart from conflicts (#120).
    - gt extension list marks a local extension whose executable
      no longer exists (#119).
    - gt schema marks date-time fields (#127).
  - Security
    - Local extensions run only when their executable, or what it
      links to, is a regular file owned by you or root that not
      every user can write to or replace (#119).
    - The commit an extension install resolves must be a full
      commit ID before it is shown or passed to git (#119).
    - --debug strips control characters from transport errors,
      which can quote server text (#119).
    - gt run download checks every artifact name before writing
      anything, also when extracting into directories (#119).
    - A job log that is missing no longer prints the server's raw
      error, which could include its storage path (#122).
  - Fixes
    - secret set and variable set refuse values that are not
      valid UTF-8 instead of silently changing them (#119).
    - gt issue create --blocked-by/--blocking refuses a missing
      issue before creating the new one (#120).
    - Pin, unpin, lock and unlock on an issue or pull request
      already in that state report it and change nothing, instead
      of a server error (#120).
    - Merging a pull request blocked by an open dependency names
      the blocking issues instead of a server error (#120).
    - gt commit pr prints the pull request without --json and
      accepts abbreviated SHAs (#120).
    - gt pr checks --required names the base branch when its
      protection requires no checks, gt status --json prints
      mentions: [] instead of null, gt pr review --pending and gt
      pr review reply report a missing body correctly, and gt
      time cancel no longer asks to discard a stopwatch that is
      not running (#120).
    - repo edit --dry-run with topic flags, and repo delete/repo
      archive with --dry-run in a clone, no longer fail (#121).
    - repo archive with several repositories checks every
      argument before archiving any, repo create --team checks
      its owner before any request, and repo list
      --archived=false is honoured (#121).
    - tag list and tag create JSON fill the tagger and
      verification fields, and tag protect warns when Gitea
      leaves out users or teams (#121).
    - A case-only rename of an organization's owner team is
      refused before it reaches Gitea, gpg-key verify accepts the
      numeric ID shown by gpg-key list, and release download
      skips an asset whose name cannot be a file name instead of
      downloading nothing (#121).
    - gt run watch and gt workflow run --follow work on servers
      that cannot list workflows or jobs, as gt run view does
      (#122).
    - gt run logs reports a job whose logs are missing, for
      example removed by retention, and goes on with the other
      jobs (#122).
    - The missing-runner hint also covers queued jobs after other
      jobs started, runner view --global no longer claims a
      runner belongs to the instance, project … --account errors
      no longer name an empty repository, and run cancel --force
      --dry-run refuses a completed run (#122).
  - Build
    - Tags such as v2.0.0-rc1 are published as pre-releases and
      no longer move the Docker latest tag, and version
      comparison orders pre-releases before their release, so gt
      upgrade and the update notice see 2.0.0 as newer than
      2.0.0-rc1 (#118).
    - The release workflow of a new Go extension (gt extension
      create --precompiled=go) installs the released gt instead
      of running go run …@latest (#118).
    - Update the Go toolchain to 1.27.4 (#109).
  - Internal
    - Transport timeout tests run on a fake clock, so they no
      longer fail on a busy machine, such as during a makepkg
      check (#110, fixes #108).
    - Dependency updates, including golang.org/x/crypto v0.59.0,
      golang.org/x/oauth2 v0.38.0 and github.com/spf13/pflag
      v1.1.0, and Gitea 28.4.0 for the integration tests (#116,
      #128).
- Don’t build on 32bit architectures (are there any developers
  using that?)
- Remove upstreamed patch:
  - unix-set-R12-before-the-ppc64x-syscall-branch.patch

