Mon Nov  9 23:03:42 UTC 2026 - Matej Cepl <mcepl@cepl.eu>

- Update to 1.2.0:
  - Features
    - gt commit reads commits on the server with list, view,
      diff, compare, status and pr, where a ref is a SHA, branch
      or tag. status exits 1 when a status failed and 8 while one
      is pending, so gt commit status main && deploy waits for
      green (#92).
    - gt commit diff and gt pr diff filter a diff with --path and
      --exclude, which take a file, a dir/ or a glob and can be
      repeated, and summarize it with --name-only, --name-status
      and --stat. What is left is still a diff that git apply
      takes (#92).
    - gt tag lists, views, creates and deletes tags without a
      clone, and protect, unprotect and protection list manage
      tag protection rules. create --message makes an annotated
      tag (#93).
    - gt branch protection list and view show the protection
      rules in the order Gitea applies them: the approvals, who
      may push, the status checks and the other protections that
      are on (#95).
    - gt activity [<owner>] shows the activity feed of a user or
      organization, yours without an owner, and gt repo activity
      that of a repository. --date keeps one day and
      --only-performed-by keeps what the user did (#100).
    - gt time start, stop, cancel and status work with the issue
      stopwatch. stop logs the elapsed time, cancel discards it
      and status lists every active stopwatch across repositories
      (#101).
    - gt pr merge --admin merges past the branch protection, for
      those who administer the repository. --match-head-commit
      SHA merges only while the head is still that commit, and
      --disable-auto cancels the merge that --auto scheduled
      (#97).
    - gt pr checks --required shows and awaits only the checks
      that the protection rule of the base branch requires, so a
      flaky optional check no longer holds --watch back (#97).
    - gt pr create --fill-first takes the title and body from the
      first commit of the branch, and --fill-verbose takes the
      body from the full message of every commit (#97).
    - gt release list takes --exclude-drafts,
      --exclude-pre-releases and --order asc|desc, which sorts by
      when the releases were published (#98).
    - gt run view --log-failed prints the logs of the jobs that
      failed or were canceled, and --job NAME|ID views one job
      or, with --log, prints its log (#98).
    - gt api --paginate --slurp prints the pages as one JSON
      array, so a script parses one document (#98).
  - Performance
    - Commands run inside a clone are about twice as fast: gt pr
      status, gt pr view, gt pr checks and gt status take roughly
      half the time. Git is asked once per command instead of up
      to 11 times, and list pages and independent searches are
      read concurrently (#103).
  - Fixes
    - gt upgrade --nightly and the nightly option of the install
      scripts no longer fail with a checksum mismatch or install
      an old build. Nightly builds are now published to
      gitea-cli/main-nightly, which is not cached for a year. The
      1.0.0 and 1.1.0 binaries still look in the old location, so
      upgrade to 1.2.0 before using --nightly again (#102).
    - On Windows, gt no longer fails to read its settings while
      another gt process is writing them (#105).
  - Documentation
    - The README lists the official gitea-cli package in the Arch
      Linux extra repository: sudo pacman -S gitea-cli (#96).
  - Internal
    - Integration tests cover gt runner, gt gpg-key, locking,
      pinning, deleting, dependencies, --template and --dry-run
      on a real Gitea (#94).
    - The golangci-lint configuration matches Gitea's, and make
      fmt runs golangci-lint fmt (#104).
    - Update charm.land/bubbletea/v2 to v2.1.1, which includes a
      security fix for terminal size reports, and
      github.com/itchyny/gojq to v0.12.20 (#107).
    - Fix a flaky test that counted requests during concurrent
      page reads (#106).

