Mon Nov  2 20:53:48 UTC 2026 - Matej Cepl <mcepl@cepl.eu>

- Update to 1.0.0:
  It is the first stable release and replaces tea as Gitea's
  official CLI.
  From now on gt follows semantic versioning: within 1.x,
  commands, flags, --json fields, exit codes and GITEA_CLI_*
  environment variables are not removed, renamed or changed in
  meaning.
  gt supports Gitea 28 and newer.
  - Features
    - gt upgrade replaces gt with its latest release, after
      verifying its SHA-256 checksum, or with the release
      --version names or the latest build of the main branch with
      --nightly. When Homebrew, a Linux package, Nix or go
      install installed gt, it names the command that upgrades it
      instead.
    - After a command, gt tells at most once a day when a newer
      release is out. It stays quiet in CI and when stdout or
      stderr is not a terminal; set GITEA_CLI_NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER
      to turn the check off.
    - gt extension installs, upgrades, runs and removes
      extensions from repositories on any Gitea instance, GitHub
      CLI extensions included. Extensions can declare top-level
      aliases in gt-extension.yml.
    - gt pr backport cherry-picks what a merged pull request
      landed onto release branches and opens a pull request for
      each, keeping going across targets when one conflicts.
    - gt project lists, views, creates, edits, closes, reopens
      and deletes project boards of a repository, an organization
      (--org) or your account (--account).
    - gt runner lists, views, enables, disables and deletes
      Actions runners, and prints the registration token, for a
      repository, an organization, your account or the instance
      (--global).
    - gt issue move moves an issue between the columns of its
      project board.
    - gt pr update-branch brings the base branch into a pull
      request, by merge or with --rebase.
    - gt issue comment attachment and gt pr comment attachment
      manage the files attached to comments.
    - --csv prints list and view output as CSV, with the same
      optional field list as --json.
    - gt pr list --local shows the pull request of each local
      branch and whether it is open, closed or merged.
  - Enhancements
    - In Gitea Actions, GITEA_TOKEN is enough: gt picks up the
      instance from the job, like gh on GitHub.
    - gt repo clone --find-instance looks the repository up on
      every instance with an account when none is selected.
    - gt pr create links the open pull request when one already
      exists for the same branches.
    - tea's command names point to their gt equivalents.
    - On servers without workflow or job listing, gt run list, gt
      run view and gt run delete warn and continue, and commands
      that need these listings say why they cannot run instead of
      "not found".
  - Fixes
    - A round of fixes went through every command group: auth,
      config and doctor, repositories, issues and milestones,
      pull requests (checkout, merge, clean, backport), Actions,
      releases, branches, wiki, packages, webhooks,
      organizations, teams, SSH keys and administration.
    - Repositories are discovered and Git is run the way Git
      itself does.
    - gt repo create --source uses the object format of the local
      repository.
    - Replacing a settings or credential file that another reader
      holds open no longer fails on Windows, and gt upgrade
      removes the replaced executable there.
  - Packaging
    - .deb, .rpm, .apk and Arch packages are published with each
      release.
    - OpenBSD builds, also installed by install.sh.
  - Security
    - Update golang.org/x/net to v0.62.0.
  - Documentation
    - Fix the PowerShell install command.
  - Internal
    - The unit tests run weekly on Windows Server.
    - Every package that does real work has more than 80% test
      coverage (87% overall), with new end-to-end tests.
    - Update gitea.dev/sdk to v1.5.0, and other dependencies.

